          <change when="2012-03-01T06:05:52.924-05:00" who="https://papyri.info/editor/users/james.cowey">Finalized - Ready. I remain unconvinced about the solution for how δέοντι καιρῷ was written by the scribe in line 11. Reviewing the image, I think that the iota has a little stroke at the bottom of the letter which might make one think that the scribe thought of writing a kappa, but it is equally possible to read δέοντι καιρῷ without positing any correction. </change>
